                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "cfd19820-2dee-3add-bce3-fa5140e61911",
                        "entry_id": "2d7e95d4-0c05-3ee9-a1e2-94519e0275dc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To decorate (wood, cloth etc.) with a purfle or ornamental border; to border."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic",
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "512bf7ed-3250-491a-aea4-b61a0286340e",
                                "sense_id": "cfd19820-2dee-3add-bce3-fa5140e61911",
                                "text": "And this was his message gretynge wel kynge Arthur in this manere wyse sayenge / that kynge Ryons had discomfyte and ouercome xj kynges /[…]/ they gaf hym their berdys clene flayne[…]/ wher for the messager came for kyng Arthurs berd / For kyng Ryons had purfyled a mantel with kynges berdes / and there lacked one place of the mantel"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "76a849f1-402d-4fd8-9893-dafc7752d2f4",
                                "sense_id": "cfd19820-2dee-3add-bce3-fa5140e61911",
                                "text": "He had a faire companion of his way, / A goodly Lady, clad in ſcarlot red, / Purfled with gold and pearle of rich aſſay, […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "20696182-d9d1-4196-99f7-54ea6f44af5b",
                                "sense_id": "cfd19820-2dee-3add-bce3-fa5140e61911",
                                "text": "It came to pass on a certain day, as he stood about the street leaning idly upon his crate, behold, there stood before him an honourable woman in a mantilla of Mosul silk, broidered with gold and bordered with brocade; her walking shoes were also purfled with gold and her hair floated in long plaits."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "78174f3d-f8bc-411d-a306-acad630eab38",
                                "sense_id": "cfd19820-2dee-3add-bce3-fa5140e61911",
                                "text": "Remembering the exchange now, Dickie smiled that winning southern-boy smile. Then he went glum again. He thumped the purfled sound board."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ed8d1a0c-8e29-3e21-a286-1770b85d9ead",
                        "entry_id": "2d7e95d4-0c05-3ee9-a1e2-94519e0275dc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To ornament with purfle."
